    "body": "A note on the cause, checked against `main` (897a820), for whoever picks this up:\n\nThe refusal is not erased by hover. Nothing in the hover path writes the status line. It is erased by the next **click** in the viewport: a short press and release inside the viewport (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/shell.rs:1160`) calls `interact::pick_at`, and `pick_model` (`crates/ui/src/interact.rs:147`) overwrites `state.status` with `selected <name>` or `no model under the cursor`. Picking a face, edge or vertex overwrites it the same way (`no face under the cursor`, `... added to ...`). Any other action that sets the status replaces it too, since `post_program_path` (`crates/ui/src/state.rs:3484`) puts the refusal only in `status`.\n\nSo the end result is the same as the issue says: the reason only lives on the shared status line until something else writes there. A fix still needs the refusal kept somewhere other than `status` (a sticky banner, or a refusal entry in the PostView pane), and a test that a viewport click after a refused post leaves the reason visible.\n\nRelated: PR #232 draws a refusal on the status strip as an alert, but it still lasts only \"until the next status replaces it\", so it doesn't cover this on its own.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
